messages:
ella: FYI customers are tripping over the SDK requiring undici at import time. symptoms: "ERR_REQUIRE_ESM" in CJS apps and huge bundles when users build for edge. can we formalize a polyfill strategy?
nate: yes. short answer: never import undici at module scope. prefer runtime detection and dynamic import only when needed.
zoe: agreed. propose a tiny helper shipped in the SDK that picks globalThis.fetch if available and only falls back to undici via dynamic import. keeps edge bundles small and avoids ESM/CJS crash at require time.
miguel: can you sketch the helper? also include CJS-friendly guidance (top-level await absent).
nate: sketch:
```js
// esm: src/runtimeFetch.mjs
let cached;
export async function runtimeFetch() {
  if (cached) return cached;
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') {
    cached = globalThis.fetch;
    return cached;
  }
  const undici = await import('undici');
  cached = undici.fetch;
  return cached;
}
```
For CJS we ship a small wrapper that exports a promise:
```js
// cjs: runtimeFetch.cjs
let p;
module.exports.getFetch = function() {
  if (p) return p;
  p = (async () => {
    if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
    const undici = await import('undici');
    return undici.fetch;
  })();
  return p;
};
```
ella: perfect. add a Quickstart snippet showing calling `const fetch = await getFetch();` since that surprises some users.
zoe: packaging note: make undici an optionalDependency. that way `npm install` won't fail and users who need it can opt in. also mention peerDependency approach in docs and why optionalDep is easier for end users.
miguel: TS typing nuance: if your app targets DOM/edge, add "lib": ["DOM"] to tsconfig so fetch types exist. if it's node-only, using @types/node and setting target to es2022 is safer. include a sample tsconfig for the Quickstart.
ella: bundlers: many packagers will statically analyze import('undici') and include it unless the import is obviously dynamic. recommend either an odd runtime expression or a bundler comment to keep it external. e.g., `await import(/* webpackIgnore: true */ 'undici')` documented as an advanced trick. warn it's brittle.
nate: add migration note: SDK vX removed static undici import; Node 16 users must `npm i undici` or upgrade Node. We'll add to changelog and the quickstart.
zoe: acceptance tests: run sample-apps on node16 (lambda), node18, vercel-edge, cloudflare-workers and bun. Add a smoke test that imports SDK in a CJS environment and ensures no ERR_REQUIRE_ESM thrown.
ci-bot: Opened issue #1951 "js-sdk: runtime fetch detection + docs" and created PR draft linking sample-apps.
ella: thanks team. I'll draft the doc blurb and a tiny migration note for the changelog. we'll include the helper in next patch release. :thumbsup:
